sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 76/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Panel A demonstrates that widening lateral angular spread theta_0 from 0 deg (fig16_odd) to 60 deg (fig17_even) switches the critical eigenbranch from odd (q* = 1.0280) to even (q* = 1.0008), and that zeroing Mexican-hat lateral inhibition (lateral_inhibition = 0) collapses the interior wavenumber peak to q_min = 0.05. Panel B continuously sweeps wavevector intersection angle theta from 0 deg to 180 deg across the 0.5*gamma_3(0) roll/lattice stability threshold for both parity branches. Deduct 14 points because all four rendered form-constant presets in kluver_presets share identical biophysical coupling parameters (parity = 'even', lateral_spread_deg = 60.0, eigen_beta = 0.35, lateral_sigma = 1.0, lateral_wide_sigma = 1.5), yielding the exact same critical wavenumber q* = 1.4475 and k* = 11 cycles; the gallery morphologies change only because the categorical pattern string and pattern_angle_deg are manually switched in planform_modes. Deduct 6 points because none of the odd-parity planform presets (fig32_square_odd, fig34_rhombic_odd, fig36_triangle_odd) are rendered to show parity-driven contour changes. Deduct 4 points because continuous scale and tuning parameters (eigen_beta, hypercolumn_mm, local_sigma_deg, lateral_wide_sigma) are never swept across a range to show monotonic control of rendered wavelength or autonomous bifurcation switching, and preset wave_count values are unused. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L288–L368: PAPER_PRESETS definitions showing identical biophysical coupling parameters across all four rendered even-branch gallery presets. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L288-L368>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L726–L790: Quantised q*-derived wavenumber ignoring preset wave_count, and manual pattern string dispatch in planform_modes. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L726-L790>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1092–L1132: Gallery loop over four hardcoded presets alongside the three-curve marginal-stability comparison (theta_0 = 0, theta_0 = 60, and I_lat = 0). <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1092-L1132>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): Exported metrics confirming all four rendered Klüver presets have identical critical_q = 1.447468 and linear_k_star = 11. — bressloff_v1_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, text/csv, 2983 B, artifact_sha256 525b9a2413dbd8214a47a3080df7ba044052ba336d68d52951443ebd03f2d8fa (sha256 525b9a2413dbd8214a47a3080df7ba044052ba336d68d52951443ebd03f2d8fa), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Parameter expressivity' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

